{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0luZGlhbl9CYW5nbGEvMjAyMC0tQmVmb3JlL0xvcmFpJTIwUGxheSUyMHRvJTIwTGl2ZSUyMCUyODIwMTUlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Lorai Play to Live","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/5zPOaeao3Ib1HzPOo6kWVsFf9HS.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/5e4lZVHakTL7ZZJfpyzNZVMU4Qy.jpg","description":"Sports minister of Westbengal sends an alcoholic retired football player (Prasenjit Chatterjee) to a politically disturbed (by Maoist activities) village of Purulia to setup a football team. The intention was to build a good activity among the poor villagers and turn their attention to football. One day, the coach is kidnapped by the Maoist (leader Parambroto Chatterjee) and rescued later. Coach decides to stay back with the villagers and teach them football, however, the ministry decides to stop the football project and the cold fight begins between the sports minister and the football coach. Sports minister decided to organize a football match between the village team vs Kolkata akadosh. If the village team could perform well government would retain the project. In the match village team perform in a extraordinary way and able to retain the project.\n\nRated UA · Released 9 Jan 2015 · India · Language: Bengali · 155 min\nStudio: GreenTouch Entertainment\n\nOn your server — Audio: Bengali (from file names)","releaseInfo":"2015","genres":["Drama","Bengali"],"imdbRating":"6.5","runtime":"155 min","cast":["Prosenjit Chatterjee","Paayel Sarkar","Indrasish Roy","Koushik Kar","Kanchan Mullick","Satyam Bhattacharya","Kharaj Mukherjee"],"director":["Parambrata Chatterjee"],"released":"2015-01-09T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Parambrata Chatterjee","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/f0vKFvgiyBvdgiXOFKpnnb6AfbG.jpg"},{"name":"Prosenjit Chatterjee","character":"Sebastian Ryan","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/vtXVSJebnsmfJC38gPy76QN3JTo.jpg"},{"name":"Paayel Sark